gh, not independently attested upstream identity.\nReport SHA256 73dd998d44e0c38550b77334e358145c1d274c745f7ef7860560ae53864eee62\n## Review\n\n**Decision: APPROVE**\n\nNo issues found.\n\n### Correct\n\n- **Clear canonical procedure and ownership.** `skills/local/meta-ads-cli/references/setup-and-commands.md:5\u201360` defines AI-managed preparation\u2014not a new CLI capability\u2014and covers one-time inspection, confirmed BM identity, authorized missing-key preparation, local token entry, and verification after \u201cdone.\u201d\n- **Credential handling is appropriately bounded.** The procedure requires exclusive creation at mode `0600` outside repositories, append-only changes for verified-missing keys, preservation of existing credentials/bindings, an empty new token value, and no guard bypass (`setup-and-commands.md:12\u201337`). This is consistent with the literal-data loader, permission/ACL checks, and duplicate rejection in `bin/secrets-env:52\u201371,103\u2013154`.\n- **The human-facing example matches the request.** `skills/local/meta-ads-cli/GUIDE.id.md:138\u2013155` presents `META_ACCESS_TOKEN_AUTOLARIS=<masukanTOKEN>`, explicitly requires local replacement, and distinguishes the example label from device-specific configuration. Existing lowercase/legacy bindings remain preserved.\n- **Documented setup outcomes match source.** Profile selection, numeric BM-ID requirements, conflict checks, and blank-token refusal are implemented in `bin/dotads-meta:38\u201392,143\u2013173`. Offline setup reports actual directories or an explicit skipped result without installing dependencies or accessing Meta (`bin/dotads-meta:1889\u20131914`). The documentation correctly avoids treating detection failure as token invalidity.\n- **English/Bahasa routing agrees.** `GUIDE.id.md:11\u201313` points to the implemented runtime rather than the historical design. `references/terminal-control.md:43\u201358` delegates to setup \u00a70 and requires real folder/assets verification. `references/account-workspace-runtime.md:26\u201331` explicitly separates AI preparation from automatic credential writes by setup/pull. These match the TASK-183 contract in `TASKS.md:13\u201317`.\n- **Scope remains focused.** The short onboarding summaries route to one checklist rather than introducing competing procedures. No misleading new helper, cross-device identity transfer, or credential-rewrite capability is claimed.\n\n### Verification limits\n\nRead-only review of the named documentation and relevant source/test definitions; no files edited, no actual secret/auth files read, and no `secrets-env` or Meta commands executed. Existing synthetic test coverage was inspected, not run. Structural/skill/link check completion remains for the parent to verify; this review does not claim those checks passed or independently prove the existing live workspace.\n\n**Merge verdict: OK for TASK-183\u2019s documentation delta.**\nExecuted documentation checker source:\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib.parse import unquote, urlsplit\nimport re\n\nroot = Path('/home/ongki/dotfiles/skills/local/meta-ads-cli')\nfiles = [root/'SKILL.md', root/'GUIDE.id.md', *[root/'references'/name for name in ('setup-and-commands.md', 'terminal-control.md', 'account-workspace-runtime.md')]]\n\ndef visible_text(file):\n    output, fenced = [], False\n    for line in file.read_text().splitlines():\n        if re.match(r'^\\s*```', line):\n            fenced = not fenced\n        elif not fenced:\n            output.append(line)\n    assert not fenced, f'Unclosed code fence: {file}'\n    return '\\n'.join(output)\n\ndef anchors(file):\n    result, counts = set(), {}\n    for heading in re.findall(r'^#{1,6}\\s+(.+?)\\s*#*$', visible_text(file), re.M):\n        slug = re.sub(r'[^\\w\\s-]', '', heading.lower())\n        slug = re.sub(r'\\s', '-', slug)\n        count = counts.get(slug, 0)\n        counts[slug] = count + 1\n        result.add(f'{slug}-{count}' if count else slug)\n    return result\n\ncount = 0\nfor file in files:\n    text = visible_text(file)\n    for target in re.findall(r'\\]\\(([^)\\s]+)\\)', text):\n        url = urlsplit(target)\n        if url.scheme or url.netloc:\n            continue\n        destination = (file.parent / unquote(url.path)).resolve() if url.path else file\n        assert destination.exists(), f'Broken link: {file.name}: {target}'\n        if url.fragment and destination.suffix == '.md':\n            assert unquote(url.fragment) in anchors(destination), f'Broken anchor: {file.name}: {target}'\n        count += 1\nprint(f'PASS: {len(files)} Meta onboarding documents; {count} relative links/anchors; balanced code fences. Structure check only, not semantic approval.')","eventHash":"5fdcb6285989d9835b16266e06974629ab9f31f2748fb56bd8726195ac3dab90","eventId":"b23f9e82280c410eb2da27d856945619","evidenceType":"declared","executed":null,"head":"8700522605d8b13b788b06eff89cf0ab3ac55836","prevEventHash":"9f14985014b68fac5abaa38d82f190d87d196c16d913a1853a0819074a1c07d7","runId":"RUN-20261104T134944Z-7200cbea","state":"READY","status":"PASS","time":"2026-11-04T13:55:32Z","type":"verification"}
